  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "You choose how many cards to discard as Colossus of the Blood Age's last ability resolves. You may choose to discard no cards and just draw a card.",
      "oracle_id": "0788fdd2-6fab-460c-b054-a736df670f96",
      "published_at": "2026-03-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you discard zero cards, you will draw one card.",
      "oracle_id": "58c131f3-c623-4324-b061-9535018676b6",
      "published_at": "2021-11-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn’t provide any additional benefit.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it’s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don’t grant bonuses to your opponents’ Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Before a player untaps their permanents during the untap step, the game checks to see if the day/night designation should change.",
      "oracle_id": "c31e9db3-5d9d-470a-871a-b4b5b0536db5",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Day and night are designations that the game itself can have. The game starts as neither. Once the game becomes day (or less commonly, night), the game will be exactly one of them—day or night—going back and forth for the rest of the game.",
      "oracle_id": "c31e9db3-5d9d-470a-871a-b4b5b0536db5",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Double-faced permanents with daybound transform to their nightbound faces as it becomes night. Similarly, double-faced permanents with nightbound transform to their daybound faces as it becomes day. This happens immediately and is not a state-based action. It happens any time it becomes day or night, not just during the untap step.",
      "oracle_id": "c31e9db3-5d9d-470a-871a-b4b5b0536db5",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If it is day, and the active player of the previous turn cast no spells during their turn, it becomes night.",
      "oracle_id": "c31e9db3-5d9d-470a-871a-b4b5b0536db5",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If it is night, and the active player of the previous turn cast two or more spells during their turn, it becomes day.",
      "oracle_id": "c31e9db3-5d9d-470a-871a-b4b5b0536db5",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If it is night, permanents with daybound that enter the battlefield without being cast will enter with their nightbound faces up.",
      "oracle_id": "c31e9db3-5d9d-470a-871a-b4b5b0536db5",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If it's neither day nor night, and a creature with daybound and a creature with nightbound somehow appear on the battlefield at the same time, it becomes day. The creature with nightbound will transform.",
      "oracle_id": "c31e9db3-5d9d-470a-871a-b4b5b0536db5",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you cast a spell with daybound during night, that spell will be front face up (that is, daybound face up) on the stack. However, it will enter the battlefield with its back face up (that is, with its nightbound face up). It won't enter with its daybound face up and then transform.",
      "oracle_id": "c31e9db3-5d9d-470a-871a-b4b5b0536db5",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Permanents with daybound and nightbound can't transform via any means other than their daybound and nightbound abilities. Notably, older cards such as Moonmist that instruct a player to transform permanents don't affect permanents with daybound or nightbound.",
      "oracle_id": "c31e9db3-5d9d-470a-871a-b4b5b0536db5",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": 1,
